#
# Single violation: a math:NormalizationDeclaration correctly naming its (source,
# target) pair through math:normalizes/math:normalizesTo, but declaring NO
# math:normalizationStrength at all — the bare, strength-less declaration the
# module.ttl math:normalizationStrength min-qualified-cardinality-1 restriction on
# math:NormalizationDeclaration exists to forbid. Before that restriction, this
# declaration satisfied NEITHER math:FalseStructuralNormalizationClaimConstraint's
# structural-strength guard NOR math:UnattributedNormalizationConstraint's
# coarser-than-structural guard (both are gated on an ASSERTED
# math:normalizationStrength before ever engaging their existential body), while
# math:UndeclaredNormalFormConstraint was ALREADY discharged by the mere presence of
# the (normalizes, normalizesTo) pair — so a strength-less, procedure-less,
# unattributed declaration satisfied the entire normal-form contract for free. It no
# longer does: the min-qualified-cardinality-1 restriction now fires a named, typed
# math:UndeclaredNormalizationStrength violation, bound through the restriction's own
# gmeow:enforcesFailureClass.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

ex:strengthlessSource a math:MathematicalExpression ;
    math:normalForm ex:strengthlessTarget ;
    math:literalValue "6"^^xsd:integer .

ex:strengthlessTarget a math:MathematicalExpression .

ex:strengthlessDecl a math:NormalizationDeclaration ;
    math:normalizes ex:strengthlessSource ;
    math:normalizesTo ex:strengthlessTarget .
